From: Max <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: fix IPQ9574 Gen3 link training for non-compliant endpoints

The Qualcomm PCIe 2.9.0 architecture used on IPQ9574 (and IPQ8074) requires
GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL and GEN3_RELATED_OFF_RXEQ_RGRDLESS_RXTS
for endpoints such as QCN9074.

In Linux 6.18, qcom_pcie_start_link unconditionally invokes
qcom_pcie_common_set_equalization(), which modifies GEN3 equalization
registers and explicitly clears GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL.
This causes receiver detection to fail (LTSSM remains in DETECT_QUIET)
and link training never completes.

Skip equalization for ops_2_9_0 and do not clear GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL
in qcom_pcie_common_set_equalization().

Signed-off-by: Max <max@maxnet.lan>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom-common.c | 1 -
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c        | 5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom-common.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom-common.c
@@ -31,7 +31,6 @@ void qcom_pcie_common_set_equalization(s
 		}
 
 		reg = dw_pcie_readl_dbi(pci, GEN3_RELATED_OFF);
-		reg &= ~GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL;
 		reg &= ~GEN3_RELATED_OFF_RATE_SHADOW_SEL_MASK;
 		reg |= FIELD_PREP(GEN3_RELATED_OFF_RATE_SHADOW_SEL_MASK,
 			  speed - PCIE_SPEED_8_0GT);
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -282,6 +282,8 @@ struct qcom_pcie {
 	bool use_pm_opp;
 };
 
+static const struct qcom_pcie_ops ops_2_9_0;
+
 #define to_qcom_pcie(x)		dev_get_drvdata((x)->dev)
 
 static void qcom_perst_assert(struct qcom_pcie *pcie, bool assert)
@@ -310,7 +312,8 @@ static int qcom_pcie_start_link(struct d
 {
 	struct qcom_pcie *pcie = to_qcom_pcie(pci);
 
-	qcom_pcie_common_set_equalization(pci);
+	if (pcie->cfg->ops != &ops_2_9_0)
+		qcom_pcie_common_set_equalization(pci);
 
 	if (pcie_link_speed[pci->max_link_speed] == PCIE_SPEED_16_0GT)
 		qcom_pcie_common_set_16gt_lane_margining(pci);
